{
  "_comment": [
    "One entry per voice named in soh/soh/Enhancements/tts/VoiceCast.cpp, then per language.",
    "model/speaker pick the voice; pitch and formant are semitones. asetrate moves both",
    "together (a physically larger speaker) and a pitch-only shift moves the fundamental",
    "alone, so the pair reaches any body size and any register.",
    "There is no default voice on purpose: a character with no entry here stays silent",
    "rather than borrowing someone else's. Navi and Malon are measured from the game's own",
    "samples (495 Hz and 297 Hz sung); the rest are picked from a pitch scan of the first",
    "300 libritts_r speakers. French has only two usable voices, so its characters are",
    "separated by pitch and formant rather than by speaker."
  ],
